{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe structural underestimation: The model consistently forecasts a slow, linear drift (approx. +0.03-0.05/day) while the market exhibits high-volatility regime shifts (e.g., sudden jumps from ~80 to ~88). Apply a regime-switching adjustment that detects breakout levels in the last 5 days and shifts the baseline forecast upward by 5-8 EUR immediately.",
    "Eliminate linear extrapolation bias: The model fails to capture mean reversion after spikes. When the true price exceeds the forecast by >3 EUR, the model must be corrected to anticipate a pullback or plateau rather than continuing the upward drift.",
    "Address lag in trend recognition: The model reacts too slowly to momentum changes. If the 3-day moving average of true outcomes rises sharply, the forecast horizon must be adjusted to reflect the new higher mean rather than the historical average.",
    "Ignore sentiment as a primary driver in this specific window: Since sentiment history is uniformly zero, do not apply sentiment-based multipliers; instead, rely strictly on technical momentum indicators to override the model's default mean-reverting logic."
  ]
}
